{"name":"Tweed Jacket","hex":"#ccb586","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tweed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coarse woolen fabric used for clothing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tweed"},{"term":"jacket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain types of outerwear.\nA piece of clothing worn on the upper body outside a shirt or blouse, often waist length to thigh length.\nA piece of a person's suit, beside trousers and, sometimes, waistcoat; coat .\nAn outer garment (usually white) intended for chefs and which may be taken to signify status.\n A vest ; a waistcoat .\n A letter jacket.","A piece of clothing worn on the upper body outside a shirt or blouse, often waist length to thigh length."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To confine (someone) to a straitjacket. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To enclose or encase in a jacket or other covering."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jacket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sport coat","blocks":[{"text":"A sport coat or sports jacket is a men's smart casual lounge jacket designed to be worn on its own without matching trousers, traditionally for sporting purposes. Styles, fabrics, colours and patterns are more varied than in most suits; sturdier and thicker fabrics are commonly used, such as corduroy, hopsack, flannel, linen, and tweed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Tailored_sport_coat_partial_lining.jpg/330px-Tailored_sport_coat_partial_lining.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sport_coat","wikidata":"Q55400351"},{"title":"Tweed","blocks":[{"text":"Tweed is a rough, woollen fabric, of a soft, open, flexible texture, resembling cheviot or homespun, but more closely woven. It is usually woven with a plain weave, twill or herringbone structure. Colour effects in the yarn may be obtained by mixing dyed wool before it is spun."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Harris_tweed.jpg/330px-Harris_tweed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tweed","wikidata":"Q40601"},{"title":"Jacket","blocks":[{"text":"A jacket is a garment for the upper body, usually extending below the hips. A jacket typically has long or short sleeves and fastens in the front or slightly on the side. Jackets without sleeves are vests. A jacket is generally lighter, tighter-fitting, and less insulating than a coat, but both are outerwear. Some jackets are fashionable, while some others serve as protective clothing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Jacket2-1.jpg/330px-Jacket2-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacket","wikidata":"Q849964"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg/500px-Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg/500px-Tweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tweed making at the Leach family woollen mill at Mochdre, Powys, Wales, 1940","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATweed_making_at_the_Leach_family_woollen_mill_at_Mochdre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Bike_in_Tweed_Stockholm_2013.jpg/500px-Bike_in_Tweed_Stockholm_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Bike_in_Tweed_Stockholm_2013.jpg/1280px-Bike_in_Tweed_Stockholm_201